-A tiered predictor design was used to test whether low-cost field screening could approximate richer hydrochemical screening. Tier 1 represented field-screening predictors and included field-measurable variables and coordinates. Tier 2 represented a reduced-chemistry tier based on selected major hydrochemical variables after target-wise leakage filtering. Tier 3 represented the broader chemistry tier, including expanded chemistry and derived ratios after leakage control. This structure allowed model performance to be compared across operationally realistic information levels, from field deployment to fuller laboratory-supported interpretation. For TDS, two reduced-tier sensitivity variants were retained: an EC-inclusive design and an EC-strict design in which EC was excluded as a conductivity proxy for TDS.
